`PR145-PubDoc-final-report` — reviewed **38449fe8bdb7549e3f83fd8f2b0e5b3a308d5965**. Two bounded findings remain:

1. **Palette:** `response_comparison.py:149` uses grey/purple/olive/blue for ECAL curves and markers. Apply the required ECAL `#cccc00` with line/marker distinctions, then regenerate SVG, PDF and provenance. :codex-file-citation{path="[redacted]" purpose="source"}

2. **Access date:** `primary_odd.access_date` says 2026-11-17, while the retained upstream inspection occurred 2026-11-15. Preserve that access date separately from the report-update date. :codex-file-citation{path="[redacted]" purpose="source"}

Otherwise, the eight-page report clearly distinguishes human-selected LAr400 from the retained800 combined-integration control, unmatched ODD markers from matched10k curves, and saved-hit H from complete-deposit A. It attributes the reported Michael Duehrssen discussion without inventing his sign-off. :codex-file-citation{path="[redacted]" purpose="source"}

Actual checks: all9 assignment hashes; all20 immutable source hashes; builder/data/producer/SVG/checkpoint bindings; historical PDF/delta preservation; all8 pages’ extracted text; 8-page/11-link counts; all8 existing renders matched independently rendered pinned PDF pixels. Visually inspected pages4–5. GitHub independently confirmed the [human comment](https://github.com/asalzburger/nodd/pull/145#issuecomment-6951330371) and distinct merge destinations for PR142/143/144.

No edits, native/MC execution or broad CI. Statistics were not independently rederived in this publication review.
